# text = Made up with curls , wreaths , wings , white bismuth , and carmine , this hopeful young person soared into so pleasing a Cupid as to constitute the chief delight of the maternal part of the spectators ; but in private , where his characteristics were a precocious cutaway coat and an extremely gruff voice , he became of the Turf , turfy said Mr . E . W . B . Childers , glancing round the room said Mr . Gradgrind Mr . Bounderby put in retorted Mr . Childers , after surveying him from head to foot said Cupid said Mr . Childers . ( Master Kidderminster was Cupid's mortal name cried Master Kidderminster , showing a very irascible temperament said Mr . Childers , raising his voice to Mr . Gradgrind asked Mr . Gradgrind , glancing at the potent Bounderby for assistance said Master Kidderminster Mr . Childers interpreted said Mr . Gradgrind Mr . E . W . B . Childers answered ejaculated Bounderby , with his laugh of laughs retorted Cupid said Mr . Gradgrind , turning , and knitting his brows on him retorted Master Kidderminster , nothing abashed asked Mr . Gradgrind , eyeing him in a sort of desperation said Mr . Childers , thrusting his young friend from the room , rather in the prairie manner continued Mr . Childers , quickly said Mr . Childers , with a nod asked Mr . Gradgrind , forcing the word out of himself , with great solemnity and reluctance said Childers Bounderby repeated said Mr . E . W . B . Childers , superciliously throwing the interpretation over his shoulder , and accompanying it with a shake of his long hair - which all shook at once interrupted Mr . Bounderby E . W . B . Childers replied pointedly , that he was not at all astonished to hear it said Bounderby retorted Mr . E . W . B . Childers , facing about remonstrated E . W . B . with stern irony replied Mr . Bounderby , rattling his money and laughing said Childers Eyeing Mr . Bounderby from head to foot again , he turned from him , as from a man finally disposed of , to Mr . Gradgrind said Mr . Gradgrind said Childers , taking a step or two to look into the empty trunk .
