# text = Sleary , who was troubled with asthma , and whose breath came far too thick and heavy for the letter s He addressed Mr . Gradgrind , who answered he returned , taking off his hat , and rubbing the lining with his pocket-handkerchief , which he kept inside for the purpose said Mr . Gradgrind said Mr . Gradgrind said Mr . Sleary , with hospitable ease said Mr . Gradgrind Here his daughter Josephine - a pretty fair-haired girl of eighteen , who had been tied on a horse at two years old , and had made a will at twelve , which she always carried about with her , expressive of her dying desire to be drawn to the grave by the two piebald ponies - cried Then came Sissy Jupe , running into the room as she had run out of it .
