# text = It must be admitted that he allowed her half a pound of tea a year , which was weak in him : first , because all gifts have an inevitable tendency to pauperise the recipient , and secondly , because his only reasonable transaction in that commodity would have been to buy it for as little as he could possibly give , and sell it for as much as he could possibly get ; it having been clearly ascertained by philosophers that in this is comprised the whole duty of man - not a part of man's duty , but the whole repeated Bitzer said Mrs .
