# text = Albeit it was as much against the precepts of his school to wonder , as it was against the doctrines of the Gradgrind College returned Tom , now actually crying ; and his tears were better than his injuries , however pitiful a figure he made A true friend thought Mr . Harthouse , lazily said Tom , grasping his hand returned the other said Tom , shaking his head dismally , and chewing rosebuds said Mr . Harthouse in conclusion , himself tossing over a rose or two , as a contribution to the island , which was always drifting to the wall as if it wanted to become a part of the mainland said Harthouse , clapping him on the shoulder again , with an air which left him at liberty to infer - as he did , poor fool - that this condition was imposed upon him in mere careless good nature to lessen his sense of obligation When Tom appeared before dinner , though his mind seemed heavy enough , his body was on the alert ; and he appeared before Mr . Bounderby came in he said , giving her his hand , and kissing her After this , there was a smile upon Louisa's face that day , for some one else .
